# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL connector credentials → the `live` test suites, and `pnpm fortnox:connect`.
#
#   cp secrets/connectors.env.example secrets/connectors.env
#   $EDITOR secrets/connectors.env
#
# ONE file for every connector, keyed <PROVIDER>_*. Each connector's live suite SKIPS
# unless its keys are complete here, so a checkout without this file stays offline and CI
# never needs it.
#
# ── This is NOT secrets/platform.<env>.env, and the difference matters ──
#
# `platform.<env>.env` is a PUSH MAP: `node scripts/secrets.mjs push` uploads every key in
# it to the deployed Cloudflare Workers. A provider credential must never take that path.
# Its home in production is a SEALED CONNECTION in the directory, opened per
# (tenant, vertical, provider) — which is what makes a leaked token cost one tenant's one
# integration instead of the fleet. A connector credential in a worker's ambient env is
# the hole #862 closed.
#
# So nothing here is ever pushed anywhere. `scripts/secrets.mjs` does not read this file.
# These values exist to point a LOCAL test at a provider's sandbox, nothing more.
#
# Point every one of these at a TEST account. Fortnox creates up to 30 test databases;
# Scrive has a testbed. `secrets/*.env` is gitignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Fortnox (accounting) ──
# CLIENT_ID / CLIENT_SECRET come from the Fortnox Developer Portal.
# TENANT_ID is the company's DatabaseNumber and is shown NOWHERE in the portal — paste the
# pair below, then run `pnpm fortnox:connect` (no flags) to complete the one-time service
# consent and print the TENANT_ID line.
FORTNOX_CLIENT_ID=
FORTNOX_CLIENT_SECRET=
FORTNOX_TENANT_ID=

# ── Scrive (e-signing) ──
# OAuth1 "personal access credentials" — four parts of ONE signature, not OAuth2 bearer.
# From Scrive's API settings. Defaults to the testbed; SCRIVE_BASE_URL overrides.
SCRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
SCRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=
SCRIVE_TOKEN_ID=
SCRIVE_TOKEN_SECRET=
# SCRIVE_BASE_URL=https://api-testbed.scrive.com
